// Pseudo-idempotent consumer outline
async function handle(msg) {
  if (await seen(msg.id)) return;
  await process(msg);
  await markSeen(msg.id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback plan under load?
- What are trade-offs of increasing partitions vs increasing consumer replicas?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to triage, choose concrete signals, and perform automated rollback under pressure without customer impact.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant latency metrics (p95/p99)
- Backlog and ingestion lag
- Feature flags and weighted traffic routing
- Grace periods and rollback gates
- Postmortem and runbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-rollback snippet
function rollbackIfNeeded(metrics, thresholds) {
  if (metrics.p95 > thresholds.p95 || metrics.backlog > thresholds.backlog) {
    enableFeatureFlag('NEW_PATH', false);
    routeTraffic(OLD_PATH_WEIGHT = 100);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this rollback plan in a staging environment?
- What telemetry would you collect for the postmortem?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to reason about cascading failures in a real-world, multi-region microservices architecture. It evaluates understanding of both preventive controls (rate limits, circuit breakers) and reactive strategies (cache bypass, warmup) with measurable SLOs and fast rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Per-endpoint rate limiting and circuit breakers for load control
- Cache warmup and controlled rollouts for spike preparation
- Backpressure and producer throttling to regulate traffic flow
- Eviction tuning and failover paths for resilience
- Automated rollback and SLO-driven incident response

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket limiter (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.refillRate = refillRate;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allowRequest() {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.refillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}
```
